          "description": "checkRunFinalizer.js adds a new branch for `reviewResult.skipped && reviewResult.reason === \"not_activated\"` placed BEFORE the existing `!reviewResult` branch. This is correct for the current code. However, the branch ordering creates a latent defect: the skip object `{ skipped: true, reason: ... }` is truthy, so if reviewPR ever returns a skip with a different reason (e.g. a future 'pillar_disabled' skip added to reviewPR, or any new structured-skip reason), it will NOT match the new branch, will NOT match `!reviewResult` (object is truthy), will NOT match `reviewResult.blocked`, and will fall into the final `else` (success) branch — which accesses `reviewResult.verdict` and `reviewResult.findings` (both undefined on a skip object). This would post a GitHub Check Run titled 'GitWire — review passed' with 'Verdict: undefined, undefined finding(s).' — a false success on a skipped review. Today reviewPR only emits reason 'not_activated', so this is not triggered yet, but the dual-gate architecture (getEffectiveReviewState already distinguishes 'pillar_disabled') makes it likely a future change adds that reason to reviewPR without updating the finalizer. The guard should match on `reviewResult.skipped` generically rather than a specific reason string.",
          "affectedPaths": [
            "packages/web/src/services/checkRunFinalizer.js"
          ],
